  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>betaincinv</keyword>
  <short_description>Inverse of the regularized incomplete beta function.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>X = betaincinv(Y, Z, W)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>X = betaincinv(Y, Z, W, type)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>Y</param_name>
      <param_description>probabilities in [0, 1]: a real single or double array.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>Z</param_name>
      <param_description>a real nonnegative array, or a scalar.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>W</param_name>
      <param_description>a real nonnegative array, or a scalar.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>type</param_name>
      <param_description><b>'lower'</b> (default) or <b>'upper'</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>X</param_name>
      <param_description>values in [0, 1] such that <b>betainc(X, Z, W, type) = Y</b>.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>X = betaincinv(Y, Z, W)</b> returns <b>X</b> such that <b>betainc(X, Z, W) = Y</b>. With <b>'upper'</b>, <b>X</b> solves <b>betainc(X, Z, W, 'upper') = Y</b>.</p>
    <p>The inputs must have the same size, or be scalars. <b>betaincinv(0, Z, W)</b> is <b>0</b> and <b>betaincinv(1, Z, W)</b> is <b>1</b>.</p>
    <p>Newton iterations on the logit <b>log(X / (1 - X))</b> start from the best of three approximations and stay inside a bracket narrowed by bisection.</p>
  </description>
